# HeartLinks ABA - Keyword Quality Summary Report
**Production-ready draft for Google Docs**
## Executive Summary
This report answers the client's main question: **which exact raw keywords are producing higher-quality Clients or Opportunities, and which exact raw keywords are mostly creating Leads, Subscribers, No-DX, out-of-target, or location-review records?**
The analysis uses 1,317 workbook records and 1,317 unique Record IDs from Jan. 1 through May 30, 2026. All keyword tables use exact raw extracted keywords only. Keywords are not cleaned, normalized, grouped, rewritten, or inferred from the Message field.
The strongest keyword trends are the terms that connect the full path: **raw keyword -> city/location -> Client or Opportunity outcome -> family inquiry theme -> market recommendation**. Across the workbook, the best signals come from ABA service intent, in-home ABA intent, autism/ASD support, localized city searches, and branded HeartLinks/Links searches when those terms reach Client or Opportunity stages.
The weaker trends are not simply low-volume terms. A keyword is marked for review when it has no Client/Opportunity signal, is at least 70% Lead/Subscriber with at least 3 lower-quality records, contains No-DX records, produces out-of-target records, or has a campaign/location match that needs review.
Subscriber-heavy keywords need context. The Indiana source-analysis reference explains that CTM can auto-create HubSpot Subscriber contacts from inbound calls, including hangups, voicemails, info-only calls, wrong numbers, and calls that did not reach intake. Those records are real signals, but they are not the same as intake-qualified leads.
## Definitions
- **Higher quality:** Client or Opportunity lifecycle stage.
- **Lower quality:** Lead or Subscriber lifecycle stage.
- **Out of target:** a lead/client/opportunity location that is outside the documented campaign target geography or is not validated by the supplied target-location references.
- **Location evidence:** ZIP match first when available; otherwise City + State match. Georgia target/range notes come from the Georgia Geo Analysis Report and workbook notes only.
- **Raw keyword rule:** `aba home`, `in home aba`, `aba therapy near me`, `aba services near me`, `links aba`, `heartlinks aba`, and similar variants remain separate if they appear separately in the workbook.
